  "id": "t2-secant-v1",
  "mechanism_class": "structural",
  "mechanism_rationale": "Second-order critic input-gradient penalties (BCap, RHBI, BISPF, EMPF) construct create_graph=True autograd graphs over 2-3 critic batches per step, costing >55% of DCGAN r256 wall time in EMPF (155.4 ms/step) and 589-3113 ms/step in RHBI/BCap due to Conv2d/BatchNorm2d double-backward FLOPs and saved activations. By Kirszbraun-Kantorovich metric Lipschitz duality, bounding multi-scale secants |D(b)-D(a)|/||b-a||_2 <= kappa across live real/fake endpoints and one detached Chebyshev-Weyl chord probe (concentrating micro-secants near endpoints to bound directional derivatives alongside macro inter-mode chords and all-pairs supremum envelopes) enforces 1-Lipschitz critic geometry using strictly 1st-order forward/backward passes.",
